---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const title = "Terms of Service — Ceche";
const description = "Terms of Service for Ceche domain appraisal platform.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-24">
    <div class="text-center" data-aos="fade-up">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-base-content/60">Last updated: July 20, 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 prose prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:font-semibold prose-a:text-primary prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline max-w-none text-base-content/80">
      <h2>Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>By accessing or using Ceche ("the Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.</p>

      <h2>Description of Service</h2>
      <p>Ceche provides domain name valuation estimates based on publicly available data and algorithmic analysis. Estimates are provided for informational purposes only and do not constitute professional or financial advice.</p>

      <h2>Use License</h2>
      <p>The Ceche CLI and TUI are distributed under the MIT License. You are free to use, modify, and distribute the software in accordance with that license.</p>
      <p>The Ceche web platform and API are provided as hosted services. You may access these services for lawful purposes only.</p>

      <h2>User Responsibilities</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the Service for any unlawful purpose or in violation of any applicable laws</li>
        <li>Attempt to circumvent rate limits, access controls, or security measures</li>
        <li>Use the Service to harass, abuse, or harm others</li>
        <li>Interfere with or disrupt the integrity or performance of the Service</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>The Ceche name, logo, and brand are trademarks. The source code is licensed under MIT. You may not use the Ceche brand to endorse or promote products without prior written permission.</p>

      <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED. CECHE DOES NOT GUARANTEE THE ACCURACY, RELIABILITY, OR COMPLETENESS OF DOMAIN VALUATIONS. VALUATIONS ARE ESTIMATES ONLY AND SHOULD NOT BE THE SOLE BASIS FOR FINANCIAL DECISIONS.</p>

      <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>In no event shall Ceche or its contributors be liable for any damages arising out of the use or inability to use the Service, including but not limited to lost profits or data.</p>

      <h2>API Terms</h2>
      <p>API access is granted on a subscription basis. You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your API keys. Abuse or excessive usage may result in rate limiting or suspension.</p>

      <h2>Termination</h2>
      <p>We reserve the right to suspend or terminate access to the Service at any time, without prior notice, for conduct that violates these Terms or is harmful to the Service or other users.</p>

      <h2>Changes to Terms</h2>
      <p>We may update these Terms from time to time. Continued use of the Service after changes constitutes acceptance of the new Terms.</p>

      <h2>Governing Law</h2>
      <p>These Terms shall be governed by the laws of the United States. Any disputes shall be resolved in the courts of the United States.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>For questions about these Terms, contact us via <a href="https://github.com/cocor-tech/Ceche/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Issues</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
